1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,560
Number three is stop trying to fit in it's a good thing to not fit in.
第三点，是别再努力迎合；她认为不合群有时是好事。

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:08,720
You know I know sometimes it can suck when you don't have like your group of friends.
没有自己的朋友圈时，有时确实会很难受。

3
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:14,600
Because on tv and on shows you constantly see girls in groups and you're like oh my gosh I want that.
因为电视剧里总看到女孩们成群结伴，你也会想拥有那样的关系。

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:20,440
It's the same thing with relationships you know if you're single you're probably thinking like oh I want love sometimes or maybe not.
恋爱也是一样，单身时你可能会想要爱情，也可能不想。

5
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:25,560
For the most part I know a lot of us may feel lonely if we don't have like a group of friends.
她知道很多人在没有朋友圈时会感到孤单。

6
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:30,200
But you start to think more as an individual when you're not in a group setting.
但她认为，不在群体环境里时，人会更独立思考。

7
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:35,720
What happens when and I'm not saying this to bash friend groups because you know if that's your thing natur really it's your thing.
她强调不是批评朋友圈；如果你自然喜欢群体相处，那就是你的偏好。

8
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:42,600
But if you don't have a friend group for example you probably have more trust in your own opinion.
如果没有固定朋友圈，比如说，你可能更信任自己的判断。

9
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:45,440
Than someone who is used to being in a group.
她把这种情况与习惯处在群体里的人作比较。

10
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:50,359
Because what happens when you are in a group is you end up conforming to each other.
因为在她看来，群体成员容易彼此趋同。

11
00:00:50,359 --> 00:00:57,280
You kind of start to become the same person the same way of thinking the same type of mindset.
你们可能开始变得相像，思考方式和心态也相似。

12
00:00:57,280 --> 00:01:04,239
And it doesn't promote individual thinking because when you voice something like an opinion for example in a group setting.
她认为这不利于独立思考；比如在群体里表达意见时……

13
00:01:04,239 --> 00:01:08,440
You end up just kind of like playing it safe and more comfortable.
你最终可能选择稳妥、让自己更舒服的说法。

14
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:12,440
It's not always easy to be your most authentic self because we conform.
做最真实的自己并不总是容易，因为人会适应群体。

15
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:15,639
It's just human nature we want to be accepted and we want to fit in.
她说想被接受、想融入是人的天性。

16
00:01:15,639 --> 00:01:21,069
And that's of course something we cannot change like to some extent it's healthy.
这也不完全能改变，她认为在某种程度上还算正常健康。

17
00:01:21,079 --> 00:01:28,959
Stop prioritizing the need to fit in you know like don't change who you are just to be liked by anybody.
但不要把合群放在首位，也别只为被喜欢就改变自己。

18
00:01:28,959 --> 00:01:32,680
When you let go of the need for approval you also free yourself.
放下寻求认可的需求，也是在让自己自由些。

19
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:39,760
From that pressure to conform into society into groups into being accepted.
她说这样能减轻迎合社会、群体和被接纳的压力。

20
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:45,359
And it really teaches you how to validate yourself without needing external validation.
你会学着肯定自己，不必总依赖外部认可。

21
00:01:45,359 --> 00:01:52,799
And also I would say by not worrying so much about fitting in you're going to have a much more unique experience with life too.
不那么担心融入，她认为也能得到更独特的人生体验。

22
00:01:52,799 --> 00:01:56,880
Learning how to meet new people like this is all very valuable skills.
学会结识新朋友，这些都是很有价值的技能。

23
00:01:56,880 --> 00:02:00,840
Think about a time where you went to an event right you bring your friend what happens.
想想你带朋友去参加一个活动，会发生什么？

24
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:05,310
Most likely you and your friend just stay in a corner and chat it up which is great.
你们多半会待在角落里聊天，这当然也很好。

25
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:11,799
But if you do that too often you also close new doors and new opportunities to meet new people.
但如果总这样，也可能错过结识新人的机会。

26
00:02:11,799 --> 00:02:15,440
Like I remember I was so intimidated to go to brand events.
我记得自己以前很害怕参加品牌活动。

27
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:18,719
And when I get invited to events they usually allow a plus one.
受邀参加活动时，通常可以带一位同行者。

28
00:02:18,719 --> 00:02:24,680
And when I would bring someone I felt like I was keeping myself in that safe comfortable feeling.
带人一起去时，我感觉是在保持那种安全、舒适的状态。

29
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:28,040
Which you know for my anxiety purposes probably was good.
对于缓解我自己的焦虑来说，这或许有好处。

30
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:35,350
But if I'm looking to grow and develop as a person it's actually better for me to be uncomfortable sometimes and go alone.
但如果目标是个人成长，她觉得自己有时独自去、接受一点不自在更好。

31
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:40,000
Which I've now started to go to events most of the time alone and I always meet new people.
现在我大多数时候独自参加活动，总能认识新朋友。

32
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,040
Be the source of your own happiness instead of relying on others to do it for you.
她建议成为自己快乐的来源，而不是全靠别人。

33
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:50,320
And also too it's really important to remember that you are the average of the five people you hang out with the most.
她还提到一种说法：你是最常相处的五个人的平均值。

34
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:54,279
So really think about where you're spending your time and your energy.
所以认真想想，你的时间和精力都花在哪里。

35
00:02:54,279 --> 00:02:59,520
The next thing I want to talk about is I wish that I knew the importance of setting boundaries.
接下来，她希望自己早点明白设立边界的重要性。

36
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:03,970
I honestly didn't even learn about setting boundaries until like 2 years ago.
她坦言，自己大约两年前才开始学习设立边界。
